-- BUILT (unit SRM22): dev runs a3 (exit 1), a4 (exit 1, placeholder table), a5 (exit 0); the final-SHA rebuild in REPORT-SRM22.md is the only final evidence.
-- SCOPE (SRM22 audits) of the new theorems: the six generic direction lemmas and `mem_seqRegs_openFlat` (Tools/ShippingSrm22Width.lean), the six helper facts about the two counterexample modules, the two counterexamples
-- and the two corollaries (Tests/Compiler/Srm22PairsTest.lean), and of the five gap definitions.
-- (1) PREMISE TABLE (index, binderInfo, name, Prop-or-data, type) equal to `Tests/Compiler/Srm22AuditExpected.lean` and `scripts/srm22/PREMISES.txt`, `S22THM` marker per theorem, literal count guard (17);
-- three semantic negative fixtures (` ∧ True` on a Prop binder, added data binder, reordered binders), each non-vacuous and rejected.  REGENERATION: build Tests.Compiler.Srm22AuditTest, then `python3 scripts/srm22/gen_audit.py LOG`.
-- (2) INDEPENDENT FULL-TYPE EXPECTED STATEMENTS: `Tests/Compiler/Srm22ExpStmt.lean`, GENERATED by scripts/srm22/gen_exp.py from scripts/srm22/EXPECTED.txt (fixed before any proof) and from the SRM20 / SRM21 SOURCE statements with the committed deletion/insertion list;
--     `isDefEq` to each final type and to each gap definition body; six wrong expected forms (direction reversed, hpost dropped, hfit deleted, hIW deleted, the gap premise hreg dropped, the SRM20 statement with hin kept) are rejected.
--     The helper theorems (mem_seqRegs_openFlat, eIn_*, eEmpty_*) were added during the proofs and are NOT in EXPECTED.txt: they appear in the premise table only.
-- (3) ONE WITNESS for the corollaries; every gap Prop is checked NOT defeq (for any parameters) to any Prop binder type of SRM20 M, SRM21 Q', SRM19 endToEnd M/Q, SRM9 hierC_at_free M/Q and of the new theorems (no relabelling).
-- (4) CLOSURE: standard axioms; forbidden old-form roots (with control); SRM20's theorem (M) / SRM21's theorem (Q') and `hin_of_hinsFit` are in the corollaries' closures.
